### TL;DR

1. **Enable terrain** (`map.setTerrain({source:'your-dem',exaggeration:1})`).  
2. **Add a sky object** (or call `map.setSky()`) with `sky-color`, `horizon-color`, `sky-horizon-blend`.  
3. **Add fog/haze** via `fog-color`, `horizon-fog-blend`, `fog-ground-blend`.  
4. Ensure the camera pitch is > 0 and you’re using a recent MapLibre version.

Follow the code snippet above, tweak the colour/fog values to your taste, and the blank page background will be replaced by a beautiful sky that fades into a soft haze at the horizon. Happy mapping!

Below is a **step-by-step recipe** that turns the empty “page background” you see above the horizon into a proper sky with a gentle haze (fog) that blends into the terrain.  
All of the pieces are native to **MapLibre GL JS** – no extra plugins are required.

---

## 1️⃣  What you need first

| Requirement | Why it matters |
|-------------|----------------|
| **MapLibre GL JS ≥ 2.4** (or any version that ships the `sky` object) | The `sky` root-level object was added after the early 2.x releases. |
| **A `raster-dem` source** and `map.setTerrain({source:…,exaggeration:…})` | The sky only renders when a 3-D terrain mesh exists. |
| **Pitch > 0** (you already have 70°) | The sky is drawn only when the camera is tilted away from nadir. |
| **A style that either (a) already contains a `sky` object or (b) you call `map.setSky()` after the map is loaded** | The sky is not a layer – it lives at the root of the style. |

If any of those are missing, the sky will never appear.

---

## 2️⃣  Add the terrain source (if you haven’t already)

```js
// 1️⃣  Add the DEM source (replace the URL with your own)
map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
  type: 'raster-dem',
  url: 'https://tiles.mapterhorn.com/tilejson.json', // <-- your DEM TileJSON
  tileSize: 256,
  // optional: encoding: 'terrarium' | 'mapbox' (match your DEM)
});

// 2️⃣  Turn the DEM into a 3-D mesh
map.setTerrain({
  source: 'terrain-dem',
  exaggeration: 1.0          // tweak later if you want more “vertical” relief
});
```

> **Tip:** Call `setTerrain` **after** the source is added and **before** you add the sky (otherwise the sky will be ignored).

---

## 3️⃣  Create the sky (the “horizon” + haze)

You have two ways to inject the sky:

| Method | When to use |
|--------|-------------|
| **`map.setSky({...})`** – programmatic, works on any map that is already loaded. | You want to add the sky after the map is created, or you are building the style dynamically. |
| **`sky` object inside the style JSON** – static, part of the initial style. | You ship a complete style file (e.g. `style.json`) and want the sky to be baked in. |

Below we show the **programmatic** approach because it works even if you are loading a style from a URL.

### 3.1  Minimal sky (just a blue gradient)

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  // 3️⃣  Add a sky with a simple blue-to-white gradient
  map.setSky({
    // The colour of the sky *above* the horizon
    'sky-color': '#199EF3',          // a calm daytime blue

    // The colour exactly at the horizon line
    'horizon-color': '#ffffff',      // bright white

    // How quickly the sky colour blends into the horizon colour
    // 0 = abrupt line, 1 = very smooth gradient
    'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5
  });
});
```

That alone will replace the white page background with a blue sky that fades into the horizon.

### 3.2  Adding fog (haze) that meets the ground

Fog is **part of the sky object** – there is no separate `setFog` method.  
You control three parameters:

| Property | Effect |
|----------|--------|
| `fog-color` | Colour of the haze (usually a desaturated version of the sky colour). |
| `horizon-fog-blend` | How quickly the fog appears as you approach the horizon (0 = no fog, 1 = fog starts right at the horizon). |
| `fog-ground-blend` | How far the fog reaches down onto the terrain (0 = fog stays high, 1 = fog reaches the ground). |

A common “ground-meeting-haze” setup looks like this:

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  map.setSky({
    'sky-color': '#199EF3',          // deep daytime blue
    'horizon-color': '#ffffff',      // bright horizon
    'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,

    // ---- Fog (haze) ----
    'fog-color': '#c0d8ff',          // a very light, slightly desaturated blue
    'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,        // fog starts a little before the horizon
    'fog-ground-blend': 0.6          // fog reaches down onto the terrain
  });
});
```

**Result:**  
* The sky fades from blue to white at the horizon.  
* A soft, semi-transparent haze begins a short distance before the horizon and gently drapes over the terrain, giving the impression of atmospheric depth.

---

## 4️⃣  Full example (everything together)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – 3D terrain with sky & fog</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@latest/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@latest/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // any base style you like
    center: [-122.447303, 37.753574], // San Francisco (example)
    zoom: 12,
    pitch: 70,          // you already have this
    bearing: 0,
    antialias: true    // needed for smooth terrain rendering
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // ---- 1️⃣  Add DEM source ----
    map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
      type: 'raster-dem',
      url: 'https://tiles.mapterhorn.com/tilejson.json', // <-- your DEM TileJSON
      tileSize: 256,
      // encoding: 'terrarium'   // uncomment if your DEM uses Terrarium encoding
    });

    // ---- 2️⃣  Enable terrain ----
    map.setTerrain({
      source: 'terrain-dem',
      exaggeration: 1.0
    });

    // ---- 3️⃣  Add sky + fog ----
    map.setSky({
      'sky-color': '#199EF3',
      'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
      'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,

      // Fog (haze) settings
      'fog-color': '#c0d8ff',
      'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,
      'fog-ground-blend': 0.6
    });

    // (Optional) make the background transparent so the sky is visible even where no tiles exist
    map.setPaintProperty('background', 'background-color', 'rgba(0,0,0,0)');
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What each part does

| Code line | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `map.setTerrain({...})` | Builds the 3-D mesh from the DEM. |
| `map.setSky({...})` | Inserts the sky object (gradient + fog). |
| `sky-color` / `horizon-color` | Define the colour of the sky and the line where it meets the ground. |
| `sky-horizon-blend` | Controls how smooth that colour transition is. |
| `fog-color` | Colour of the atmospheric haze. |
| `horizon-fog-blend` | How early the haze appears before the horizon. |
| `fog-ground-blend` | How far the haze reaches down onto the terrain. |
| `map.setPaintProperty('background', …)` (optional) | Makes the map’s background transparent so the sky shows even in empty corners. |

---

## 5️⃣  Common pitfalls & how to fix them

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **Sky never appears (still white page)** | *`map.setSky` called before the map is fully loaded* or *MapLibre version < 2.4* | Call `setSky` inside `map.on('load', …)` and verify you are using a recent MapLibre build. |
| **Fog looks like a solid colour covering the whole view** | `horizon-fog-blend` set to `0` or `fog-ground-blend` set to `1` | Increase `horizon-fog-blend` (e.g., `0.3`) and lower `fog-ground-blend` (e.g., `0.6`). |
| **Sky disappears when I change the style** | The new style does not contain a `sky` object and you didn’t re-call `setSky` | After `map.setStyle(...)` wait for the `styledata` event, then call `setSky` again. |
| **Terrain looks flat even with pitch** | `map.setTerrain` not called *or* `exaggeration` set to `0` | Ensure `setTerrain` runs after the DEM source is added, and use a non-zero `exaggeration`. |
| **Horizon line is too sharp** | `sky-horizon-blend` is `0` | Raise it to `0.4–0.7` for a smoother gradient. |

---

## 6️⃣  Tweaking for different moods

| Desired look | Suggested changes |
|--------------|-------------------|
| **Sunset / dusk** | `sky-color: '#ff9e80'`, `horizon-color: '#ffcc80'`, lower `sky-horizon-blend` (0.3) and add a deeper `fog-color: '#ffb380'`. |
| **Night sky** | `sky-color: '#0b1d3c'`, `horizon-color: '#1e3a8a'`, `fog-color: '#0b1d3c'` (very dark), increase `horizon-fog-blend` for a thin mist. |
| **Heavy mountain haze** | Keep `sky-color` bright, but set `fog-color` to a desaturated gray (`#c0c0c0`) and raise `fog-ground-blend` to `0.8`. |
| **Clear alpine** | Very low fog: `horizon-fog-blend: 0.05`, `fog-ground-blend: 0.2`. |

Feel free to experiment – the sky and fog are cheap to render, so you can animate them (e.g., change `sky-color` over time) without hurting performance.

---

## 7️⃣  Quick checklist (copy-paste into your code)

```js
// After map is loaded
map.on('load', () => {
  // 1️⃣ DEM source
  map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
    type: 'raster-dem',
    url: 'YOUR_DEM_TILEJSON_URL',
    tileSize: 256
  });

  // 2️⃣ Enable terrain
  map.setTerrain({ source: 'terrain-dem', exaggeration: 1 });

  // 3️⃣ Add sky + fog
  map.setSky({
    'sky-color': '#199EF3',
    'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
    'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
    'fog-color': '#c0d8ff',
    'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,
    'fog-ground-blend': 0.6
  });
});
```

That’s all you need. Once the sky object is present, the area above the horizon will no longer be the plain page background – you’ll see a proper sky with a gentle haze that meets the terrain.

Happy mapping! 🌄🚀
